# Ship weapon ports
signal-port-name-weapon-fire = Manually fire weapon
signal-port-description-weapon-fire = Fires the weapon once when it receives a pulse.
signal-port-name-weapon-aim = Aim weapon
signal-port-description-weapon-aim = Aims the weapon toward where the gunnery computer selects.
signal-port-name-weapon-autofire = Toggle autofire
signal-port-description-weapon-autofire = Toggles on/off the weapon's autofire mode.
signal-port-name-weapon-autofire = Toggle autofire
signal-port-description-weapon-autofire = Toggles on/off the weapon's autofire mode.

# These are mainly used by gunner computers
signal-source-name-weapon-fire = Fire button
signal-source-description-weapon-fire = Emits a pulse when the fire button is pressed.
signal-source-name-weapon-aim = Aim control
signal-source-description-weapon-aim = Emits a pulse when the computer selects a position to aim at.
signal-source-name-weapon-autofire = Autofire button
signal-source-description-weapon-autofire = Emits a pulse when the computer's "autofire" button is pressed.

# Data ports / radar ports
signal-port-name-weapon-gunnery-data = Gunnery data (receiver)
signal-port-description-weapon-gunnery-data = Receives weapon data, which the computer can use to organize it all.

signal-port-name-weapon-radar-data = Radar data (receiver)
signal-port-description-weapon-radar-data = Receives preliminary radar data, which the computer can use to visualize it all.

signal-source-name-weapon-gunnery-data = Gunnery data (transmitter)
signal-source-description-weapon-gunnery-data = Transmits data regarding this weapon in a rude manner.

signal-source-name-weapon-radar-data = Radar data (transmitter)
signal-source-description-weapon-radar-data = Transmits radar data (missiles, bullets) in a mean manner.
